{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers","id":641212,"title":"Why Cavaliers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Cavaliers of Mars"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-26T23:39:21-07:00","id":641212,"title":"Why Cavaliers?","content":"Rose, what was it that made you want to make a game about Cavaliers? Why on Mars?<br /> <br /> Did you watch The Princess Bride one time too many? Had fond memories of a game of 7th Sea? Read some inspiring description of the landscapes on Mars?<br /> <br /> What spurred the project?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T00:55:11-07:00","id":641266,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the seed of inspiration was &quot;well if Mars has canals, it must have had Venice!&quot; Beyond that, there's some definite Edgar Rice Burroughs influence, but with the twist of being more rapier and doublet than gladius and sandals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T09:12:46-07:00","id":641714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers#post641212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose, what was it that made you want to make a game about Cavaliers? Why on Mars?<br /> <br /> Did you watch The Princess Bride one time too many? Had fond memories of a game of 7th Sea? Read some inspiring description of the landscapes on Mars?<br /> <br /> What spurred the project?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really hard to say. The basic aesthetic of the setting came to me all at once when I was brainstorming for a game to run with my friends over Thanksgiving weekend. Here's the &quot;trailer&quot; I sent them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> [sound of howling wind]<br /> <br /> On a world beyond time<br /> <br /> [zooming across a landscape of red sand]<br /> <br /> In a land beyond the desert<br /> <br /> [shifting, zooming along a canal]<br /> <br /> In a city without compassion<br /> <br /> [the ziggurat looms in the distance, the sprawl of the city rushes by below us as we zoom in on its top]<br /> <br /> [we settle and circle on a priest atop the ziggurat. his clothes are yellow silk, but he\u2019s showing plenty of muscled, shining skin. his head is unnaturally oval. he\u2019s covered in tattoos and ritual paint designs, and stands with a wicked knife over a silent-screaming sacrificial victim]<br /> <br /> [closeup on the victim\u2019s face]<br /> <br /> [shots of the shouting crowd, eager for blood]<br /> <br /> [close on the knife, then on the roaring priest as he stabs it downwards]<br /> <br /> [lock on the knife as it stabs downward \u2014 and is blocked by a rapier shining in the martian noon \u2014 sparks flying from the impact]<br /> <br /> [close on the face of a man with a beard and an extravagant hat. he\u2019s holding the rapier]<br /> <br /> [music with a pumping drumbeat kicks in]<br /> <br /> [another scene of the swordsman in the hat, this time walking through a crowd of ragged but stylish people that parts like the red sea. he\u2019s got a babe in one arm and a flintlock laser pistol in the other]<br /> <br /> [cut to a hover chariot racing through the desert. a woman on a mechanical horse pulls even with it. she aims and fires a flintlaser. the chariot spins, flips over, cut to the woman\u2019s horse rearing over the driver]<br /> <br /> Die for honor<br /> <br /> [the bearded swordsman plummeting from a great height]<br /> <br /> [a gorilla artillery man firing a howitzer at figures mounted on flying beasts]<br /> <br /> [the bearded man pulling a dancing girl to him by the waist]<br /> <br /> Live for everything<br /> <br /> [silhouetted figures duelling with swords on a telegraph wire above the city]<br /> <br /> [the gunslinger girl crushing a guy\u2019s mouth to hers]<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cavaliers of Mars</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Around the same time, I was reading <i>Royal Flash</i> and <i>Captain Alatriste</i>, and the swashbuckling vibe really got into my head. Once I had the notion of swords in search of adventure, Fafhrd and the Gray Mouser and <i>Gentlemen of the Road</i> came into the picture. And obviously if I'm writing about a dying world, I'm going to look to Jack Vance's first two Dying Earth collections.<br /> <br /> Where did the name &quot;Cavaliers&quot; come from? I actually have no idea. It just sort of fit, and as soon as I thought of it, I knew what I wanted to do with the cavaliers in the setting.<br /> <br /> And Mars? I just like Mars a lot. The landscape is beautiful, and it's hard not to think what it would look like traced by canals and dotted with cities.<br /> <br /> I wrote part of a short story called &quot;A Thief of Mars&quot; shortly thereafter, which nailed down a few particulars of the setting. I also had an RPGnet thread going for a bit where I brainstormed things like some of the careers and cities. And from there on, it took on a life of its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:46:27-07:00","id":641809,"title":"","content":"Given the similar concepts, is it safe to assume you also drew inspiration from Edgar Rice Burroughs' Warlord of Mars books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T11:02:32-07:00","id":641828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=641809#post641809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the similar concepts, is it safe to assume you also drew inspiration from Edgar Rice Burroughs' Warlord of Mars books?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some clear love letters to Burroughs in the game. Among other things, the wealth of exotic beasts are inspired by Burroughs and Vance. But the setting and tone more closely follow the generation of planetary romance writers who followed in Burroughs' footsteps. Specifically, Leigh Brackett's Eric John Stark adventures (&quot;Black Amazon of Mars,&quot; &quot;The Secret of Sinharat,&quot; <i>The Ginger Star</i>, etc) better capture the atmosphere of our Mars.<br /> <br /> (Read those if you haven't, they're amazing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:33:13-07:00","id":642094,"title":"","content":"Swashbuckling is an odd genre for me. My only real exposure to it is through 7th Sea and when I play that I keep focusing in on Germany in the 30 Years War and the monsters in the forests and dark places and spectacularly missing the point...<br /> <br /> And the Princess Bride but that's meant to be a send up of the Genre.<br /> <br /> Did you end up running your game over Thanksgiving? Do you feel the ideas have evolved away from your initial inspiration or has it kept fairly (flint)laser focused?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:18:22-07:00","id":642139,"title":"","content":"There is always the three musketeers, and if you are looking at games flashing blades, honor + intrigue and my personal favorite All for one: Regime Dioblique(aka musketeers as a hunter organization basically)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T17:58:28-07:00","id":642270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=641828#post641828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are some clear love letters to Burroughs in the game. Among other things, the wealth of exotic beasts are inspired by Burroughs and Vance. But the setting and tone more closely follow the generation of planetary romance writers who followed in Burroughs' footsteps. Specifically, Leigh Brackett's Eric John Stark adventures (&quot;Black Amazon of Mars,&quot; &quot;The Secret of Sinharat,&quot; <i>The Ginger Star</i>, etc) better capture the atmosphere of our Mars.<br /> <br /> (Read those if you haven't, they're amazing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I surely will!<br /> <br /> I've been on something of a classics kick in the pulp fantasy genre of late. Just picked up a pretty good compilation of the original Conan stories. Got my eye on a compilation of the first five Warlord of Mars books. I'll add these titles to my list as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T21:49:59-07:00","id":642586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=642094#post642094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you end up running your game over Thanksgiving? Do you feel the ideas have evolved away from your initial inspiration or has it kept fairly (flint)laser focused?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, and although a lot of the basic ethos and aesthetic has remained the same, the setting's developed a lot. I've found more literary inspiration, I've brought in a writer who does better creatures than me, and instead of the two city-states I had in my initial conception, I've now got I think 15.<br /> <br /> When I think of movie swashbuckling, I think movies with Basil Rathbone and Errol Flynn. Those are the flashy side of <i>Cavaliers</i>. Then you've got the Alatriste novels which are sort of the hardboiled side of swashbuckling, and <i>Gentlemen of the Road</i> which is very much in the wandering swords genre. And then to just go in a completely out there direction, you've got <i>The Manuscript Found in Saragossa</i> and <i>Dictionary of the Khazars</i>.<br /> <br /> Really, if there's honor or cunning, intrigue or swords, I'm there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T01:09:58-07:00","id":642721,"title":"","content":"Do you plan on including more sci-fi style things or is it mostly just Renaissance/Fantasy with a sci-fi veneer?<br /> <br /> I.e.: would we be seeing stories about hacking computer networks from a remote data tap or would the Cavaliers style thief approach a door and take out their clockmakers kit to twiddle with brass springs and cogs to unlock the countess's fiendish trap?<br /> <br /> I once heard someone describe Swashbuckling as Western Wuxia, which I thought was pretty apt. Fairly free spirited/minded individuals with their personal codes and ethics making their way through a world of high action and conflict arising from their beliefs and lifestyles. Though, less of the rebellion against authority streak.<br /> <br /> Oh, one more mechanically minded question. Is armour relevant? It's something that has always annoyed me about 7th Sea. No one wears armour (except the magic stuff) because apparently guns made it obsolete. Despite the game focusing around sword duels. Oh. And small stuff like armoured knights with pistols fighting in caracolle being you know...kind of a thing.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Pappenheim_Curassiers.PNG/220px-Pappenheim_Curassiers.PNG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So, can I have a Cavalier on a steel horse with a carbine and pistols wearing gleaming cuirass ride into the martian sunset and have it mean something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T11:11:32-07:00","id":643192,"title":"","content":"The game includes a career called Fixer, which is someone who makes/repairs/modifies mechanical wonders. These are generally one-offs; the Arbiter's telescope in Zodiac is one of a kind... if you really want one, you should track down the Fixer's last surviving apprentice, who by the way is in trouble with a polar ice merchant...<br /> <br /> There's no network hacking. Most of the Big Sci-Fi elements are in the past of the setting, with the modern day being Renaissance with glimmers of greater things created by this generation's geniuses.<br /> <br /> Currently, armor is a thing which exists in the setting, but there's no mechanical benefit for it. That might change based on playtesting, but in the game right now gear is really important for what it enables you to do (my glass knife poisons people) than adding to or reducing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T13:04:36-07:00","id":643301,"title":"","content":"How is the Wushu System? I am not quite familar with it myself, but I am curious in new systems particularly rules lite ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T14:34:24-07:00","id":643406,"title":"","content":"So so so...Alexander Dumas in space?<br /> <br /> I'm game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T21:40:40-07:00","id":643742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=643406#post643406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So so so...Alexander Dumas in space?<br /> <br /> I'm game!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well... on Mars... which is no more &quot;in space&quot; than &quot;on Earth&quot; is... technically speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T09:32:26-07:00","id":644321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=643742#post643742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well... on Mars... which is no more &quot;in space&quot; than &quot;on Earth&quot; is... technically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming we're not going to accidentally commandeer a dilapidated rocket and go tearing off into the exosphere.<br /> <br /> This is a mistake.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:35:28-07:00","id":644587,"title":"","content":"Is there anything you've added in that you wold have sworn never would be there when you started out? Or an idea you were certain would see print but ended up not fitting in after all?<br /> <br /> I'm getting a Numenera vibe with the way the sci-fi is in the past and one of a kind wonders. Though with the theoretical ability to recreate them that departs from Numenera fairly considerably.<br /> <br /> Is there a 'magic' expy or is the strangeness just the wildlife of Mars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T15:56:30-07:00","id":644691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=644587#post644587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything you've added in that you wold have sworn never would be there when you started out? Or an idea you were certain would see print but ended up not fitting in after all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing really comes to mind. Although originally there were mechanical horses, and those aren't really around anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=644587#post644587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a 'magic' expy or is the strangeness just the wildlife of Mars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certain abilities, such as the psychic powers of the adept career, astrology, and the aforementioned fixing are classed by the book as &quot;uncanny.&quot; Some things happen that don't have easy explanations, and Martians also have a wide variety of superstitions that we don't say are right or wrong. In general, we as writers treat the beliefs of our Martian characters with respect, even when there's no mechanic that clearly proves or disproves that belief.<br /> <br /> But as far as actual schools of sorcery in the vein of some other fantasy settings, no, there isn't an equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T06:50:15-07:00","id":645368,"title":"","content":"Are there the equivalent of Martian gypsies roaming the canals, rumoured to be the heirs to an ancient legacy and with mysterious powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6557-rhebeqah","name":"Rhebeqah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T02:09:37-07:00","id":646452,"title":"","content":"Given the source material - any plan to address &quot;Earthmen&quot; in the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T08:15:37-07:00","id":646758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=646452#post646452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the source material - any plan to address &quot;Earthmen&quot; in the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very unlikely. To Martians, Earth is the blue star of ill-omen.<br /> <br /> That's not to say there's never been travel between other worlds. Deep in the Labyrinth of Night dwells the witch-queen of the Shadowed Citadel, wanderer or exile from the amber star Venus. And if you spend the time to understand an oleph's sibilant almost-language, it will tell you that it comes from someplace Other, and that its time as a beast of burden on Mars is merely an illusion from which it will eventually return.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhebeqah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=645368#post645368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there the equivalent of Martian gypsies roaming the canals, rumoured to be the heirs to an ancient legacy and with mysterious powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>The canals are one of Mars' great mysteries, a legacy of the vanished First Martians. Their general routes are known, and the flow of water is reliable (if often insufficient) in most places. But no trip up or down the canals is quite the same as any other. The paths seem to shift, sometimes being longer or shorter than before, and sometimes taking you through dark tunnels in which time is... unreliable. Canal sailors and pirates have their own languages and lore, and if you listen to one long enough, you might hear speculation that a great machine toils in the heart of the world, causing the routes to shift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T17:39:36-07:00","id":647448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=646758#post646758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not to say there's never been travel between other worlds. Deep in the Labyrinth of Night dwells the witch-queen of the Shadowed Citadel, wanderer or exile from the amber star Venus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the unshakable image that she's &quot;angelic&quot; in appearance, but her wings are useless in Mars' thinner atmosphere.<br /> <br /> Are you planning on using Earth's planet names in the finished product? &quot;Martians&quot; call Mars &quot;Mars&quot; - not and equivalent of Barsoom/Malacandra/Tyrr?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T19:37:58-07:00","id":647601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=647448#post647448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you planning on using Earth's planet names in the finished product? &quot;Martians&quot; call Mars &quot;Mars&quot; - not and equivalent of Barsoom/Malacandra/Tyrr?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It was the most straightforward thing to do during early development of the setting, and it stuck around. I really can't think of my Mars as anything but &quot;Mars&quot; at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T20:03:35-07:00","id":647613,"title":"","content":"Cool - I mean I understand the logic, as obviously we're translating the language the characters are speaking to English (or whatever given Earth language is used by a given gaming group) anyway. I think I'll be calling their world &quot;Ren&quot; at my own table, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T20:56:01-07:00","id":647643,"title":"","content":"I could have done what <i>Dictionary of Mu</i> did with its Marr'd and Urt and so on. I thought that worked nicely. <i>Dictionary</i> is pretty much the best Martian roleplaying game, but I don't want to retread it.<br /> <br /> Although Judd and I worked things out so that <i>Dictionary</i> and <i>Cavaliers</i> do share one piece of mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T21:19:50-07:00","id":647650,"title":"","content":"The Damsel Messiah I assume?<br /> <br /> Edit: Is the Sorcerer rpg book necessary for mechanics for Dictionary of Mu? Because I'm tracking down the latter, and want to know if I'll also need the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-01-2015, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T21:34:08-07:00","id":647655,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Damsel Messiah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For <i>Dictionary of Mu</i>, you need <i>Sorcerer</i>, and you'll probably want the excellent <i>Sorcerer and Sword</i>. That's if you want to play it as designed, but the setting is actually quite viable outside of <i>Sorcerer</i>'s framework, and the only mechanics in the book are stat blocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T15:37:17-07:00","id":648414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=646758#post646758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very unlikely. To Martians, Earth is the blue star of ill-omen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of tempted to turn the script and have a Confederate Veteran antagonist...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T10:38:50-07:00","id":652761,"title":"","content":"Would Planet Krishna of the <i>Viagens Interplanetarias</i> series make a reasonable reference milieu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:37:39-07:00","id":657036,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Just the fact that there is a game played solely on Mars makes me giddy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T11:28:48-07:00","id":660924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=652761#post652761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Planet Krishna of the <i>Viagens Interplanetarias</i> series make a reasonable reference milieu?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't actually read them, but from what I've heard, they seem relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:28:09-07:00","id":668162,"title":"","content":"I've not read a whole heap about CoM so far, but what little I have sounds a bit like Fading Suns? Only redder, drier and dustier? I have never read any, as far as I can tell, of the novels etc mentioned through this thread as inspirational/source material<br /> <br /> Likely seen as a sin by others, but I generally only read RPGs these days, my days of slogging through novels is past I think as I tend to get a bit into them and find something to hate/that makes no sense etc; I find most novels and even short stories so boring and very dry. As a child I read voraciously, often stuff I shouldn't read, but none of it fantasy/sci-fantasy. Mostly straight up sci-fi, horror or comedic stuff.<br /> <br /> Will a knowledge of Fading Suns and historical texts fare me well in the CoM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:37:33-07:00","id":668451,"title":"","content":"It's not much like <i>Fading Suns</i>. Have you ever seen <i>Captain Blood</i> or <i>The Adventures of Don Juan</i>, both starring Errol Flynn? It's more like those, although the setting itself is much weirder.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't really need a background in the inspirational material to enjoy the game, though. It's very up-front about what the setting's like and what you do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T06:42:19-07:00","id":669608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=668451#post668451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not much like <i>Fading Suns</i>. Have you ever seen <i>Captain Blood</i> or <i>The Adventures of Don Juan</i>, both starring Errol Flynn? It's more like those, although the setting itself is much weirder.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't really need a background in the inspirational material to enjoy the game, though. It's very up-front about what the setting's like and what you do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>After I posted the above I pondered, momentarily, my love of books in my youth and started a thread on RPG.net about inspirational materials and the lists that get dropped into most RPGs. 99% of the time I don't think I've even heard of the authors let alone the actual works .... so I'm going to remedy that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not seen either of the Errol Flynn movies (Bit old-school for my normal tastes, i tend to stick the 90's and more present stuff for films - I'm a heathen I know!). But ... again it can't hurt to expand my horizons and get out of the rut of horror/zombie/kids/big-budget-eye-candy type movies I normally stick too. I'll keep en eye out for DVDs on ebay!<br /> <br /> So glad I got a tablet a few months back. All my RPGs in one place and now a growing list (And small collection) of novels/shorts and articles to read.<br /> <br /> I shall follow CoM development eagerly. Really interested as to what happened to Earth/on Earth whilst Mars was colonised etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T21:49:12-07:00","id":671670,"title":"","content":"Where does the setting fall by default on cynicism v. optimism? On the one hand a lot of the talk of the NPCs makes me think of something dark and gritty and tragic in a pulp fantasy mold, but the talk of PCs makes me think fighting for truth and love and justice. Somewhere in between probably?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T21:55:57-07:00","id":671672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/cavaliers-of-mars/641212-why-cavaliers?p=671670#post671670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does the setting fall by default on cynicism v. optimism? On the one hand a lot of the talk of the NPCs makes me think of something dark and gritty and tragic in a pulp fantasy mold, but the talk of PCs makes me think fighting for truth and love and justice. Somewhere in between probably?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a mix. The actual backdrop of the game can get pretty tragic. But there's also life and color and romance for the PCs to get mixed up in. The plot hooks reflect this blend, with some dark undertones and some reckless adventure.<br /> <br /> If you look at the Apprentice from &quot;The Apprentice's Tale,&quot; she's a woman very conscious of the coming end of the world, in large part because as she writes it she's just lost her father figure. But then if you turn around and read &quot;Two Swords of Mars,&quot; you have two characters reveling in life on the razor's edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:48:14-07:00","id":672482,"title":"","content":"I think that is one of the strengths of the game. Mars' trajectory is a dramatic, tragic one but there is still a great deal of life left on the planet, burning bright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}